What this means for your account

Observability is moving to its own subscription. If your account is on:

Workers Paid: Your account will automatically receive an Observability Paid subscription. Starting December 1, usage beyond the included allowances will be billed under the new subscription at the rates below.
Enterprise: Your existing contract terms apply until renewal, when the new pricing takes effect.
No Workers Paid plan or Enterprise contract: Your account stays on Observability Free, with no Observability charges. Ingestion pauses when the daily limit is reached and resumes when it resets.
New pricing

Usage will be measured by GB ingested and GB-month stored, rather than the number of events.

Plan	Included ingestion	Included storage / retention	Additional usage
Free	0.5 GB per day	Seven-day retention included	Not available
Paid	50 GB per billing cycle	10 GB-month per billing cycle	$0.25 per additional GB ingested;
$0.10 per additional GB-month stored
Ingestion and storage charges apply only to data ingested on or after December 1, 2026. Earlier usage will not be charged retroactively.

Covered datasets

Your account’s included allowances are shared across:

Cloudflare Traces
Workers Logs and Workers Traces
Containers logs
R2 Data Access Logs
AI Gateway logs
Issues
Any new datasets added to Cloudflare Observability that you enable will also use this pricing model.

